    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "those are good points. but can u expand more on the entitlement part? like, how exactly does the lack of boundaries lead to them becoming entitled adults? i want to make sure i can explain that specific link clearly in my video so people really get why the old ways are better.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When parents constantly prioritize a child's immediate emotional comfort over necessary behavioral correction, they inadvertently teach the child that their desires supersede established rules. This constant accommodation signals that the world bends to their needs, fostering a belief that they are exempt from societal expectations. Without the firm boundary of \"no,\" children learn that persistence in demanding something will eventually yield results, which is the very definition of entitlement. This lack of friction prevents the development of the crucial skill of accepting limitations.",
      "source": "target",
